SUMMARY:Advent Wreath Making
DESCRIPTION:  \nIn the Parish House Forum Room \nCelebrate the first Sunday of Advent with an afternoon of festive fun! Families\, parishioners\, and friends of all ages are invited to create their own Advent wreath. We’ll provide the wreath frames\, fresh greens\, candles\, and all the materials you need to make a beautiful wreath to light at home throughout the Advent season as we prepare for the birth of Christ. \nIf you have a wreath frame from last year\, please bring it along to use again! \nA pizza lunch will be provided. All ages are welcome! \nRegistration is kindly requested to help us plan for the afternoon. An at-the-door $10 – $20 donation for wreath-making supplies and lunch would be appreciated! \nPlease click here to RSVP by Monday\, November 23.
URL:https://www.saintjameslancaster.org/event/advent-wreath-making/
LOCATION:Saint James Parish House\, 119 North Duke Street\, Lancaster\, PA\, 17602\, United States
CATEGORIES:Advent,Children Youth & Families
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://www.saintjameslancaster.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/2026-Wreath-making-FEATURED-IMAGE-2.jpg
GEO:40.0404103;-76.303616
